From 3c776501103e0db1a5a8c3ca700ad07a83d13a78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 11:30:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0147 -- wave-52 mode_draw_scene decomp
 instrumentation

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/WAVE-52-DECOMP-DESIGN.md sec.3 contract.
Instrumentation-ONLY cycle-0 iter (no lever, no single-lever conflict)
that decomposes the ~9 ms un-instrumented scrolling-frame slice on the
canonical KPI scene. Env gate SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MDS_DECOMP (strict "1",
cached-at-boot; default OFF). Design doc draft-named the patch
"-mds-scroll-decomp"; team-lead's task name "-mds-decomp-instr" is
canonical.

n=70/100 COVERAGE-GAP ROOT-CAUSE -- CAUSE (a), structurally proven:
The [mode-draw-scene-stat] n=70/100 vs [mode-tick-stat] n=100 gap is
NOT escaped brackets (cause b). Proof: ModeTickTimer wraps
tickfunctions[game.mode].OnTick() once per Game::tick(), ALL modes ->
n=100. The W22.5 MdsClear/MdsTilemapBg/... sub-brackets fire ONLY
inside DrawScene(), which is called ONLY from game_tick_normal()
(GM_NORMAL's OnTick) unconditionally, and DrawScene()'s first statement
(MdsClearTimer) is unconditionally placed with no early-return above
it. Therefore n<100 is ONLY possible when fewer than 100 ticks ran
game_tick_normal -- i.e. ticks where game.mode != GM_NORMAL
(GM_INVENTORY / GM_MAP_SYSTEM / GM_NONE during switchstage) or
game.paused. n=70 = exactly 70 GM_NORMAL scene-draws; it is COMPLETE
coverage of every scene-draw that happened. The ~9 ms is entirely
inside those scene-draws, not hiding behind the gap. Fix: patch 0147
emits per 100 SCENE-DRAWS (a consistent denominator), not per 100
flips. No bracket-placement change needed.

WHAT IT EMITS (per 100-scene-draws block, engine <TAG>.LOG, LOG_INFO):
- [mds-decomp-stat n=N phase=<...> min/med/mean/p95/max ms] x12 --
  the full mode_draw_scene decomposition re-reported self-sufficiently
  (mode_draw_scene parent, mds_clear, mds_tilemap_bg, mdt_bg_backdrop,
  mdt_bg_tilelayer, mds_object_loop, mds_player, mds_tilemap_fg,
  mds_carets_water_floats, mds_residual, bd_cache_blit, bd_full_redraw).
  Reuses _compute_flip_phase_stats (wave-20 STAT machinery).
- [mds-decomp-route ... bd_route_cache/direct/paid_both tm_route_*] --
  the wave-48 cache-thrash double-pay check. bd_paid_both expected ~0.
- [mds-decomp-pass ... pass_clear_bytes / pass_backdrop_bytes /
  pass_bg_tile_scan_bytes / pass_fg_sprite_scan_bytes /
  avg_passes_per_scene_x10] -- per-layer framebuffer-write bytes for
  the MODEX-PLAN sec.5.7 redundant-pass premise.
- [mds-decomp-frames ... static_frames / scroll_frames] -- per-block
  camera-delta cluster split.

DESIGN DECISIONS (flush-instr-acked):
- (i+) self-contained: 0147 emits the full decomposition on its OWN
  gate; the existing [mode-draw-scene-stat] (MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR) is
  NOT retrofitted -- no cross-gate behavior change, no audit-flush
  desync. PLAY1 = MDS_DECOMP=1 only.
- Option A (acked) -- instead of a parallel set of 0147 timers, the
  ~10 existing W22A/W22.5/W29 timer-destructor gates in
  diagnostic_timers.h are WIDENED from `if (!INSTR) return;` to
  `if (!INSTR && !mds_decomp_active()) return;`, with each timer's
  sample-array write kept INSTR-only (`if (INSTR && idx<N)`). The
  per-tick `g_*_dt_this_tick` VALUES are thus published under
  MDS_DECOMP; 0147 re-reads them. ZERO double-instrumentation -- there
  is only ever one timer per region. This is the wave-25
  g_mds_tfg_loop_active gate-widening pattern generalized.
- bd_*/tm_* (acked narrowing) -- instead of threading 3 fragile RAII
  timers through map_draw_backdrop()'s ~600 lines / ~7 scrolltype
  branches: bd_cache_blit is timed at the Renderer::drawCachedBackdrop
  + drawCachedBackdropClipped chokepoint; bd_full_redraw is DERIVED
  (W29 MdtBgBackdropTimer total - bd_cache_blit); the bd_route_* +
  bd_paid_both counters are DERIVED at record time from
  (bd_cache_blit, mdt_bg_backdrop_dt) -- so map.cpp needs ZERO
  instrumentation. tm_* counters derived from the tilemap-cache
  killswitch state (cache is default-OFF -> route=direct).

VERIFY-POINT 1 (flush-instr self-check) -- REGRESSION SAFETY: the
widened gate `if (!INSTR && !mds_decomp_active()) return;` + the
sample-array write kept `if (INSTR && ...)` makes existing
W22A/W22.5/W29 instrumented-iter output BYTE-IDENTICAL when MDS_DECOMP
is off: when INSTR is on / MDS_DECOMP off the dt write + sample write
both execute exactly as before; when both off the destructor early-
returns exactly as before. Only new behavior is the MDS_DECOMP-on dt
publish.

VERIFY-POINT 2 -- dt READ/RESET ordering: 0147's record hook
(NXE::Diag::mds_decomp_on_scene_draw) is called from game_tick_normal()
AFTER the W22.5 + W29 residual blocks -- i.e. after every Mds*Timer /
Mdt*Timer destructor has fired at its DrawScene() sub-bracket scope
exit and written its g_*_dt_this_tick, and BEFORE Game::tick()'s
next-tick reset cluster. The hook reads fresh per-tick values, never
stale or doubled.

PER-LAYER BYTE NAMING (flush-instr-specified): clear + backdrop are
full opaque writes -> rect-area == bytes WRITTEN, exact
(pass_clear_bytes / pass_backdrop_bytes). bg + fg are colorkey blits
-> rect-area == bytes SCANNED/addressed, an upper bound -> named
pass_bg_tile_scan_bytes / pass_fg_sprite_scan_bytes. Accounting is one
`+= cols*rows` per blit CALL in _blit_indexed / _blit_indexed_mirrored
(tag-attributed via g_mds_decomp_pass set by DrawScene at each layer
boundary), + clearScreen + drawCachedBackdrop[/Clipped]. ZERO
per-pixel work (the wave-51 patch-0146 cost-overrun lesson).

COST: ~12 array stores + a handful of ops per scene-draw + one
`+= cols*rows` per blit call. Budget < 0.1 ms/flip; PLAY2 (clean)
confirms the Heisenberg cost. When MDS_DECOMP is off every counter /
timer / array is untouched (cached-bool gate).

FILES: src/Utils/diagnostic_timers.h (mds_decomp_active +
mds_decomp_on_scene_draw decls + MdsDecompPass enum + g_mds_decomp_pass
extern; 10 timer-gate widenings), src/graphics/Renderer.cpp (gate def,
0147 storage + record/emit, blit + clearScreen + cached-backdrop byte
hooks, banner, NXE::Diag wrappers), src/game.cpp (per-scene-draw record
hook + 4 pass-tag sets in DrawScene).

